#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_tautology

#% text
# `is_tautology(e)` tells whether the Boolean expression `e` is true for every assignment of `true` and `false` to its variables (the symbols in it, at most 20); `is_tautology(e, vars)` takes the variables given. It stays unevaluated when some value is neither true nor false.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_tautology(a or not a)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_tautology(implies(a and b, a))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_tautology(a or b)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_satisfiable`, `boolean_table`, `equivalent`
